# qkt Bybit project

This project was generated by `qkt create template --kind bybit`.

It starts a QKT daemon wired directly to Bybit REST. There is no gateway service.
Testnet is enabled by default.

Read `CONFIG.md` for a plain-English explanation of `.env`,
`docker-compose.yml`, `qkt.config.yaml`, Bybit credentials, alerts, and state.

## First Run

```bash
cp .env.example .env
$EDITOR .env
docker compose --env-file .env config --quiet
make up
make status
```

## Environment Values

Start with Bybit testnet credentials:

```dotenv
QKT_IMAGE_TAG=v{{QKT_VERSION}}
BYBIT_TESTNET=true
BYBIT_API_KEY=
BYBIT_API_SECRET=
```

Optional Telegram alerts:

```dotenv
TELEGRAM_ENABLED=false
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
```

Set `BYBIT_TESTNET=false` only after you have validated the strategy and intend
to connect to real Bybit funds.

Keep `.env` out of Git.

## Commands

Use these commands from the project directory:

```bash
make up                         # start the QKT daemon
make logs                       # tail daemon logs
make status                     # show deployed strategies
make deploy STRAT=ema_cross     # deploy strategies/ema_cross.qkt
make resync-dry-run STRAT=ema_cross
make resync STRAT=ema_cross
make reconcile STRAT=ema_cross
make stop STRAT=ema_cross
make down                       # stop containers without deleting state
```

## Strategy Flow

1. Use testnet credentials first.
2. Review and backtest the strategy outside this deployment repo.
3. Copy the live-ready `.qkt` file into `strategies/`.
4. Deploy with `make deploy STRAT=<name>`.
5. For edits, run `make resync-dry-run`, then `make resync`, then `make reconcile`.

